1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:03,360
Hi everyone. If you haven't yet seen our

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:05,040
video on recurrent schedules, I

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,120
recommend watching that first. It covers

4
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:09,120
the basics of setting up tasks to repeat

5
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:11,519
automatically. In this video, we'll

6
00:00:11,519 --> 00:00:13,599
focus on the new update, custom

7
00:00:13,599 --> 00:00:16,480
recurring schedules. Sometimes your

8
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,560
routines don't fit into daily, weekly,

9
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:21,199
or monthly presets. That's where custom

10
00:00:21,199 --> 00:00:23,199
comes in. It gives you full flexibility

11
00:00:23,199 --> 00:00:25,680
to stop exactly the interval you need.

12
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:28,320
To use it, choose a task you want. Open

13
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:31,199
the expanded menu. Click schedule.

14
00:00:31,199 --> 00:00:33,520
Select the date of the task and click

15
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,680
next. At the bottom of the recurrent

16
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:38,320
schedule options, you'll see custom.

17
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,079
Select it for the most flexible way to

18
00:00:40,079 --> 00:00:43,360
set repeating tasks. So with custom, you

19
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:46,559
set two things. The time interval, days,

20
00:00:46,559 --> 00:00:49,840
weeks, month or years, and the number of

21
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,559
intervals. For example, we have every

22
00:00:52,559 --> 00:00:54,559
one day selected. So the task will

23
00:00:54,559 --> 00:00:57,360
repeat daily. Change it to every 3 days.

24
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:59,120
and Blitz will schedule this task for

25
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,760
every third day. A small tip line under

26
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:03,600
the settings explains your choice in

27
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,400
plain words as in this case every three

28
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,880
days. This makes it easy to double check

29
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:11,520
your setup before saving. When you

30
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:13,680
choose weeks as an interval, you also

31
00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:15,840
get to pick the exact week days you want

32
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:18,960
the task to repeat on. Let's say we set

33
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:21,600
it to repeat every four weeks and select

34
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:24,400
Monday and Friday. The summary below

35
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,280
confirms it. every four weeks on Monday,

36
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:30,240
Friday. To remove a week day, just click

37
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:33,200
it again. For month, you get a different

38
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,759
type of control than with weeks. After

39
00:01:35,759 --> 00:01:37,439
choosing the interval, you can decide

40
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:39,280
whether the task repeats on the same

41
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:42,159
date you chose each month, for example,

42
00:01:42,159 --> 00:01:44,560
the 14th, or on the same day of the

43
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,280
week, like every second Sunday. This is

44
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,520
especially useful for monthly meetings

45
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:51,600
or deadlines that always fall on a

46
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,320
specific weekday. For years, the setup

47
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,640
is simple. The task repeats on the same

48
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:58,479
date and you can adjust the number of

49
00:01:58,479 --> 00:02:01,600
years. So, if you set every four years,

50
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,680
the task will appear again on the date

51
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,840
four years later. That's some real

52
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:08,080
long-term planning.

53
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:10,319
Once you've chosen your settings, click

54
00:02:10,319 --> 00:02:12,480
schedule and Blitz will generate child

55
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:14,400
tasks just like with regular recurrent

56
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,000
schedules.

57
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,599
Custom recurrent schedules give you

58
00:02:17,599 --> 00:02:19,680
maximum flexibility for handling the

59
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:22,480
rhythms of your work. Try it out and

60
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:24,080
make your task management even more

61
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:27,120
precise. If this video was helpful,

62
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,440
check out our other tutorials and join

63
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,959
the Discord community where you can

64
00:02:30,959 --> 00:02:33,120
share your productivity strategies, get

65
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,160
feedback, and connect with fellow users.

66
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:39,560
Happy blitzing.